  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_11' aria-label=\" Tirith Kumar & Ors. versus Daduram & Ors. pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('11','2024','2024_12_665_679',''); ><font size='4'> <strong>TIRITH KUMAR & ORS.<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>DADURAM & ORS. </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2024] 12 S.C.R. 665</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010007292024></button></font><br><strong>Coram : C.T. RAVIKUMAR<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, SANJAY KAROL</strong><br> Issue for Consideration Whether the Hindu Succession Act, 1956 could be applied to the parties to the instant lis. Headnotes&dagger; Hindu Succession Act, 1956 &ndash; s.2(2) &ndash; Application of the Act &ndash; Constitution of India &ndash; Articles 366(25), 341, 342 &ndash; Central Provinces belonged to Sawara tribe, a notified scheduled tribe and thus, the HSA, 1956 does not apply to them &ndash; Granted a portion as property to M&rsquo;s daughters and their descendants (respondents) on the grounds of justice, equity and good conscience &ndash; Correctness: Held: HSA, 1956<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 19-12-2024</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CIVIL APPEAL No. 13516/2024</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Dismissed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('11','2024','2024_12_665_679','','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('11','20